                <pb facs="0552" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg540"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221 Dahl, Harold/31: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seville</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-20T13:00:00+01:00">August 20, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 20—12:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My August 4, noon, Harold Dahl. Commanding General, Seville, today expressed firm
                    opinion that Dahl would not be shot even though tried but would be
                    exchanged.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
